1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward was the son of John Mann and his wife Amey Ryves. Although he was the fifth son, he appears to have inherited the majority of his father's estate with his older stepbrothers William, John and Thomas, receiving little or not
2 CONC hing and his older brother Bartholomew receiving a smaller bequest and only on condition that he gave up a previous claim to money from their mothers estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Career
2 CONT
2 CONT Like his father, he was a merchant and was active in local affairs in Poole becoming a Freeman in 1585 and Mayor in 1589. He was MP for the town in 1589, 1593 and 1604 and held a number of positions within Dorset and became a memb
2 CONC er of Merchant's asscociations including the Spanish company in 1604 and the French company in 1611
2 CONT
2 CONT "Edward Man of Poole in Dorset son of John Man claimed the freedom by virtue of a clause in the charter of 1577, 'because his father was an auncient trader into Spaine before Anno 1568 and was lyving when the said charter was grau
2 CONC nted, the same being testified in open court'. Also .... They were both admitted, paying 6s. 8d. each and taking their oaths as freemen by ancient trade" Death and Will Edward wrote his will on 15th September 1622 'being Sicke but
2 CONC  of pefect memory' He made bequests of 20s to the church in Poole and 20s to the poor of Poole. 10s to Mr Nicholas Jefferys preacher of gods worde in poole ... to preach at my buryall. 20s to each of three Overseers my cosen Mr Ri
2 CONC chard Swayne of Blanford esquire, my cozen Mr Anthonny Weekes of Salisbury Esquier, my cosen Mt Richard Rives of Christ(?) oxford gent and my brother in lawe Mr Lewes Pope of Taunton, Merchant The rest of his estate was left to hi
2 CONC s wife Elinor who was also executrix. He appointed other relatives as executors Other members of the extended family were also witnesses John Ryves Thomas Salman John Ryves, Ro. Ryves The signature on the will was Edward Mann (tho
2 CONC ugh the scribe copying the will used a single n)
2 CONT
2 CONT The will was proved on 24 January 1623  Unfortunately the Poole parish register for this date is very damaged and most of the entries lost. However a memorial brass records his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT HERE LYETH THE BODY OF EDWARD MAN OF THIS TOWN AND COUNTY OF POOLE, MARCHANT WHOE DIED DECEMBER XX11 MDCXX11. HE LEFT TWOESONS AND FOWER DAUGHTERS HIS BELOVED WIFE ELENOR MADE THIS MEMORIAL OF HIM
2 CONT
2 CONT This marchant Man purchased a Jewel rare When to gain Christ (God man) he took care
2 CONT
2 CONT Note on Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Hambleton's book records dates of baptisms, marriages and deaths transcribed from what is suggested is an original document in the family. It differs from the History of Parliament account in the name of Edward's wives. His
2 CONC tory of Parliament says that his second wife was a sister of Lewis Pope MP from Taunton. Edward's will does indeed refer to his brother in lawe, Lewis Pope but this could refer to one of his siblings husbands (further research is 
2 CONC needed)
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a wealth of information on John Man and his family in the book cited below, including names of godparents for children, locations of baptism, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Will of John Mann full transcription ↑ 'Register Book: 1605, October-December', in The Spanish Company, ed. Pauline Croft (London, 1973), pp. 58-72. British History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/london-record-soc/vol9/
2 CONC pp58-72 [accessed 13 July 2016]. ↑ John Ferris MAN, Edward (c.1549-1622), of Poole, Dorset in The History of Parliament: the House of Commons 1604-1629, ed. Andrew Thrush and John P. Ferris, 2010 http://www.historyofparliamentonli
2 CONC ne.org/volume/1604-1629/member/man-edward-1549-1622#footnote15_kj78t3c ↑ National Archives, Will of Edward Man or Mann, Merchant of Poole, Dorset PROB 11/141/52 http://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/D910638 also viewa
2 CONC ble on ancestry.co.uk ↑ John Hutchins The History and Antiquities of the County of Dorset Third edition, corrected, augmented, and improved by William Shipp and James Whitworth Hodson 1861-73 vol p 47 ↑ Needles, Samuel Hambleton R
2 CONC ecord of the Man, Needles (Nedels) and Hambleton families...1495-1876 https://archive.org/stream/recordofmanneedl00need#page/n23/mode/2up Some information on the Man family comes from a book that purportedly transcribes journals m
2 CONC ade by John Man, Edward Man and other Man family members, from the time period: Samuel
