1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==[http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Gyllenstierna_af_Lundholm_nr_3 '''Erik Eriksson den äldre, till Demstrup'''] på Jutland, Kråkerum i Mönsterås socken och Fågelvik i Tryserums socken (båda i Kalm.) samt St. Bj
2 CONC urum i Bjurums socken Skaraborgs län] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 1'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Erik Eriksson the elder, ((son of Erik Nielssen Gyllenstjerne ), to Demstrup in Jutland''', Kråkerum in Mönsterås parish and Fågelvik in Tryserum parish (both in Kalm.) as well as St. Bjurum in Bjurum parish Skaraborg county. C
2 CONC ame to Sweden and got 1446 take over his father-in-law's fiefdom of Öland with Borgholm castle 38 1449-02-25 and riksråd 1450-05-13 King Karl Knutsson's courtier 1450. Envoy to the meeting with the Danes in Halmstad s. Envoy to Ki
2 CONC ng Christian I in Denmark 1453-05-07 Lagman i Tio härads s . Became at the handover of Borgholm Castle to the Danes on 10-10-1456 Abducted in Danish captivity and lost the office of lawman and Kråkerum's estate at the accession of
2 CONC  Christian I in Sweden. Envoy to the meeting with the Danes in Halmstad 1468-10-20. Regained the office of lawman in 1468 the Riksdag and King Kristian 1471-09-08 and to the peace treaties with the Danes in Kalmar 1472-07-02, 1473
2 CONC -08-17 and 1474-08-19. During his last years, he had Stäkeholm county (Tjust, Kinds and Ydre härader) as a fief until his death. Died 1477. He changed the color of the star in the coat of arms from silver to gold [RHKn]. '''Marrie
2 CONC d 1446-09-29 at Svartsjö Castle to Kristina Karlsdotter ,''' born 1432(?) and who was still a widow in 1492, but inheritance after her was held 1500-01-25, daughter of King Karl VIII Knutsson (Farmer) and his 1st wife Birgitta Tur
2 CONC esdotter ( Bielke ).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Carin''' died young.
2 CONT * '''Margaret''' died young.
2 CONT * '''Lisbet''' died young.
2 CONT * '''Abraham Eriksson .''' Hövidsman in Kalmar. Died 1514. to Demstrup and Assarbo. Armsman 1480. Courtier at Kalmar 1497-07-22–1503-09-10. Later stayed mostly in Denmark. Death 4 1514-02-09. His tombstone is kept in Skara Cathedr
2 CONC al 4 . Married after 1502 to Elsa Laxmand , died 1546-12-31 and buried in Valby church in Denmark 2 , daughter of the Danish chief court officer Poul Laxmand to Walden and his 1st wife Inger Holgersdotter Munk (of the Lange family
2 CONC ).
2 CONT * '''Nils Eriksson .''' Knight and Councillor. Died 1495. to Fågelvik in Tryserum's parish, Kalmar län. Was knighted and councilor 1482-08-17. Received a lifetime grant of Kastelholm county in 1485 and was sent s. Oh. with an auxi
2 CONC liary force to Riga against the German orders. Hövidsman on Åland 1491-03-20. Hövidsman at Viborg 1491-09-03. Died there in the spring of 1495 [ 6 ]. Married 1487-10-00 to Sigrid Eskilsdotter in her 2nd marriage (married 1st 1475-
2 CONC 01-15 to the knight and councilor Magnus Karlsson to Eka, died 1484), died in the fall of 1527 probably at Gäddeholm (now Tureholm) in Trosa national assembly Södermanland county and buried in Trosa church, daughter of the knight 
2 CONC and councilor Eskil Isaksson ( Banér ) and his 1st wife Cecilia Haraldsdotter (Gren) . Mrs. Sigrid was imprisoned by the cow. Christian II 1520-11-07 and was taken in 1521 together with her daughter Christina and several other dis
2 CONC tinguished women to Copenhagen, where she was kept until the beginning of 1524. Through her 1st marriage, she became the grandmother of King Gustaf I and through her 2nd marriage mother of Christina Gyllenstierna.
2 CONT * '''Erik Eriksson the younger .''' Knight and Councillor. Died 1502. to Fågelvik in Tryserum parish Kalmar county and Vinstorp in Dalum parish Älvsborg county. Had in 1485 in fief Gäsene and Ås' hrad in Västergötland 24 . Was cou
2 CONC ncilor in 1489 and chieftain at Nyköping castle in 1490. Palace bailiff in Stockholm 43 1490-08-11–1491-08-17. Hövidsman at Stäkeholm Castle 44 1493-02-11–1498. Participated on 1495-08-21 in the Kalmar meeting and on 1497-03-13 in
2 CONC  the truce negotiations between the Swedish Riksdag and Sten Sture. Celebrated p. Oh. King Hans and at his coronation became s. Oh. 29/11 knight. Hövidsman at Älvsborg in 1499. Joined 1501-09-00 in the rebellion against King Hans.
2 CONC  Lawman in Västergötland 1502-01-00. Surrendered Älvsborg Castle to Prince Christian of Denmark p. Oh. 18/7 and was beaten to death the following day 4 by the Västgöta common people, because he does not seem to have sufficiently p
2 CONC rovided for the defense of the fortress. His tombstone can be found in Skara Cathedral [ 6 ]. Married before 45 1493-03-11 to Anna Karlsdotter ( Vinstorpaätten ) in her 2nd marriage [married 1st 1488-06-30 to the Riksrådet and höv
2 CONC idsmann Erik Karlsson ( Vasa ) in his 2nd marriage (married 1st at the latest in 1466 with Iliana Nilsdotter, daughter of the Riksdag Nils Jönsson ( Oxenstierna ) and his 3rd wife Carin Sture), during a forced stay with the priest
2 CONC  in Överselö in Södermanland so badly wounded on 1491-03-20 that he died a few days later], died in 1552 and buried in Dalum's church 40 Älvsborg County, daughter of the Riksrad Karl Bengtsson, still in Vinstorp, and Karin Lagesdo
2 CONC tter (Sparre).
2 CONT * '''Brigitta ,''' died young.
2 CONT * '''Knut Eriksson .''' Mentioned only in the maternal grandfather's, con. Karl Knutsson's testament in 1470, when he receives "a red winged coat, trimmed with ermine and red wing for a shirt and a band of Kastidorian stone".
2 CONT * '''Kerstin Eriksdotter ,''' lived as a widow at St. Bjurum 1 yet 1500-01-25. Married 1473-01-23 to the knight, councilor and lawman in Närke Hans Åkesson (Tott), to Bjurum and Frötuna, died 1492-12-20 at Bosgården in Frölunda pa
2 CONC rish Älvsborg county, shot dead by a farmer. 2
2 CONT * '''Görvel Eriksdotter ,''' died approx. 1495. Married in 1488 to the governor of Akershus, the knight and councilor Knut Alfsson ( Tre roros ) in his 1st marriage [married 2nd to Metta Ivarsdotter, who lived in Denmark as late a
2 CONC s 1525, in her 2nd marriage (married 1: o with Norwegian councilor Anders von Bergen, died 1491. Married 3rd 1504-11-17 with the regent, knight and councilor Svante Nilsson (Sture), in his 2nd marriage, died 1512), daughter of Iva
2 CONC r Jenssen (Dyre), who brought two horns in the coat of arms, and Christina Pedersdotter Oxe to Assarbo] , murdered during lease 1502-08-18 at Akershus. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Noteringar''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Eriksson, svensk-dansk storman, svensk rikshovmästare, född i Demstrup, Danmark, död 1477. Han var son till lagmannen Erik Nielsen och måg till Karl Knutsson Bonde och är anfader för den svenska grenen av huset Gyllenstierna.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik övertog 1446 sin svärfars pantlän Öland med Borgholms slott. Överlämnades till danskarna 1456 och bortfördes i fångenskap. Han var ofta anlitad som sändebud vid fredsförhandlingar både före och efter fångenskapen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Källa: Elgenstierna och Dick Harrison - Karl Knutsson
2 CONT
2 CONT
