1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN MOWAT OF HOUGALAND===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Mowat of Hougaland is the eldest son of Andrew Mowat of Hougaland and his wife Ursula Tulloch. He died in August 1617. [https://archive.org/stream/TheCountyFamiliesOfTheShetlandIslands/The%20County%20Families%20of%20the%20
2 CONC Shetland%20Islands#page/n108/mode/1up The County Families of the Shetland Islands]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Shetland Sasines===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 5 March 1623 Jean Mowat and her husband David Heart sold the twelve merk land of Brewik, in the Shetland parish of Northmaven, to Mitchell Sinclair of Aeth and his wife Agnes Mowat. This land was given to Jean Mowat by her d
2 CONC eceased father John Mowat of Hwgoland. [http://www.vsnrweb-publications.org.uk/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20records/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20Records%20Vol%20II.pdf Shetland Sasines]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 18 June 1624, at a court held at St. Magnus Cathedral in Kirkwall, Orkney, the twenty merk udal land of Wester Hougoland, the fifteen merk udal lands of Stenhous with the Holme thereof, together with the fifteen merk udal la
2 CONC nd of Ollaberrie, all of which are located in the Shetland parish of Northmaven, were apprised from Andrew Mowat, eldest lawful son and heir of the deceased John Mowat of Howgoland at the instance of David Hereot, for not entering
2 CONC  as heir to his father. [http://www.vsnrweb-publications.org.uk/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20records/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20Records%20Vol%20II.pdf Shetland Sasines]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===NOTES===
2 CONT
2 CONT John Mowat, of Ollaberry (while his father lived)14, of Hugoland20. Died in August 1617. Married before 1597 13 Christian Stewart, natural daughter of Robert, Earl of Orkney.
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Andrew, see IV.25
2 CONT 2.John.26 3.Jean, married David Heart, sheriff-clerk of Orkney and Shetland. 4.Catherine, married Hugh Sinclair in Damsay, Orkney.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.cosoft.org/mowat/hugoland.html
2 CONT
2 CONT John Mowat of Ollaberry, later of Hugolnad (born circa. 1564)  http://www.enotes.com/topic/Anders_Mowatt_of_Hugoland
2 CONT
2 CONT A source on the internet shows that John Mowat (d. 1617) of Ollaberry was married by 1597 to "Christian Stewart, natural daughter of Robert, Earl of Orkney," and had a daughter "Jean, married David Heart, sheriff-clerk of Orkney a
2 CONC nd Shetland."  Is the sheriff-clerk the same person as the "writer" and notary public? 
2 CONT
