1 OCCU Rigsadmiral, regeringsmedlem, godsejer, lensmandrigsråd
1 TITL Adm.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ove Gjedde=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ove_Gjedde '''Ove Gjedde'''] was a Danish nobleman and Admiral of the Realm (Rigsadmiral). He established the Danish colony at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tharangambadi Tharangambadi] and construc
2 CONC ted [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Dansborg Fort Dansborg] as the base for Danish settlement. He was a member of the interim government that followed the death of King [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_IV_of_Denmark ''
2 CONC 'Christian IV'''] and which imposed restrictions (Haandfæstning) on his successor [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_III_of_Denmark King '''Frederick III'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Early years===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gjedde was born''' at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomarps_Kungsg%C3%A5rd_Castle Tomarps] (Tomarps Kungsgård) at Åstorp in Scania while it was still Danish. He was the son of '''Brostrup Gjedde''' and '''Dorthe Pallesdatter U
2 CONC lfeldt'''. He studied at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sor%C3%B8_Academy Sorø Academy]. He completed a tour to Germany and the Netherlands. Returning in 1616, he was appointed secretary of the Danish Chancellor.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Career===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In March 1618''', Gjedde commanded an expedition to India and Ceylon to establish a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danish_overseas_colonies Danish colony] that could be used as a base for the China and East Indies trade of the 
2 CONC [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danish_East_India_Company Danish East India Company]. His fleet consisted of the Danish naval ships Elefanten and David, the yacht Øresund, and the merchant ships Kiøbenhavn and Christian. He establi
2 CONC shed Fort Dansborg at Tranquebar, which would remain a Danish colony for 200 years. Gjedde returned in March 1622 and was appointed lord of Brunla len (now in Akershus). In 1637, he received Tønsberg len (now Vestfold).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gjedde acquired land''' properties in Norway, and was a central participant in the mining industry, and also became a partner in the silver mining venture of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kongsberg_Silver_Mines Kongsberg Sølvv
2 CONC erk], which was founded in 1623 and formally established by royal resolution in the spring of 1624 when king Christian IV himself came to inspect the newly discovered silver deposits in Sandsvær. When the silver mine company was t
2 CONC ransformed into a private partnership in 1628, Ove Gjedde got a 25% share and from 1630 he was its director. In 1657, he established the iron foundry Ulefos Jernværk at Ulefoss in Nome, together with his brother in law Preben von 
2 CONC Ahnen.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1628, he was appointed''' Lieutenant Colonel of Akershus Regiment. He participated in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torstenson_War Torstenson War] (1643-1645) as an admiral and in 1645 he was made Admiral of the Realm (
2 CONC Rigsadmiral). In 1648 he was granted the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helsingborg fiefdom] of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helsingborg Helsingborg] Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Later years===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''After the''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Roskilde '''peace in Roskilde'''], Denmark lost Scania to Sweden. When king [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_X_Gustav_of_Sweden '''Charles X Gustav'''] of Sweden broke
2 CONC  the peace of 1658, Ove Gjedde was taken prisoner, during a visit to Helsingborg. He was first sent to prison in Helsingborg castle, and later sent to Malmö. In 1660 he was released during prisoner exchanges between Sweden and Den
2 CONC mark. At the time Gjedde was an old and physically weak man, but although he had already commissioned a grave monument in Helsingborg, because this had now become Swedish, when he died he was buried in the crypt of [https://en.wik
2 CONC ipedia.org/wiki/Roskilde_Cathedral Roskilde Cathedral]. The legend says that, "''His bones after the Roskilde peace never found rest, after Scania became Swedish''" (Danish: hans ben efter Roskildefreden fandt aldrig hvile, efter 
2 CONC Skåne var blevet svensk). Gjedde died at Copenhagen in 1660.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Personal life===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1622, Gjedde''' married '''Dorothy Knudsdatter Urne''' (1600-1667), daughter of Knud Axelsen Urne til Årsmarke (1564-1622) and Margrethe Eilersdatter Grubbe til Alslev (1568-1654). His wife was a sister of Christoffer Urne (
2 CONC 1593-1663) who served as Steward of Norway. They were the parents of several children including Knud Ovessøn Gjedde and Brostrup Gjedde both of who served as County governors in Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dorte Gjedde''' (1625-?)
2 CONT * '''Brostrup Gjedde''' (1628-1668)
2 CONT * '''Margrethe Gjedde''' (16??-1706)
2 CONT * '''Merete Gjedde''' (16??-1689)
2 CONT * '''Regitze Sophie Gjedde''' (1634-1653)
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knud_Ovess%C3%B8n_Gjedde '''Knud Ovessøn Gjedde'''] (1635-1708)
2 CONT * '''Frederick Eiler Gjedde''' (1641-1717)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Adelsvapen===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/G%C3%A4dda_nr_27 '''Ove Giedde, till Tommerup'''], Vrams Gunnarstorp, Herrestad, Lövestad, Hovdala, Maglö, Tullesbo, Dragsholm, S:t Olov, Hellerup, östro och Uttersjö. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Född 1594-12-17''' på [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomarps_kungsg%C3%A5rd Tommerup]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gick i''' [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sor%C3%B8_Akademi Sorö skola] 1609-1612. Reste utomlands i fem år, först studerande vid olika universitet, därefter i krigstjänst i Holland och Tyskland. Sekreterare i danska k. kansliet
2 CONC  1616-1618. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Chef för en flotta''' till Ostindien, varvid Trankebar erövrades 1618. Lehnsman över Brunlaug och Nummedalen 1622. Kapten för ett av honom värvat kompani i kriget mot kejsaren 1624. Direktör för norska bergverken 1630. Lehnsman
2 CONC  över Tönsberg 1637. Landskommissarie 1639. Lehnsman på Bratsberg 1640-1650. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Överstelöjtnant vid''' Akershusiska regementet. Amiral över en flotta 1644. Riksråd och riksamiral 1645. Landskommissarie på Jylland 1647. Riddare vid konung Fredrik III:s kröning 1648. Lehnsman på Herrevadskloster 1649-1650, p
2 CONC å Hälsingborg 1650-1658 och på Hald 1658. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Död 1660-12-19'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1622-09-01''' på Kronborg med '''Dorte Urne''', född 1600-07-19, död 1667-07-06 och begraven s. å. 7/8 i Roskilde domkyrka, dotter av befallningsmannen Knud Axelson Urne och Margrete Grubbe.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Varia===
